## Approach

Louvain community detection on the weighted undirected file adjacency graph, integrated into the indexing pipeline after graph analysis. Edge weight = count of cross-file resolved refs per file pair (each resolved ref has ambiguity=1, so weight = 1/1 = 1 per ref; the formula generalizes when multi-candidate resolution is added later). First-run path only: if the `components` table is empty, create components from clusters; if populated, skip (reconciliation is sutra/46). Resolution parameter auto-tunes across candidate γ values by default, overridable via `.sutra/components.toml`.

No external graph library needed — Louvain operates directly on the existing adjacency data via `HashMap`. UUID v7 crate is already in Cargo.toml.

